3. Item (2): NBSP name -- FAIL
   Present and exercised:
   - The throwaway probe zz_nbsp_probe_test.go (removed afterwards; diff -rq rc=0) printed:
       "PROBE nbspName bytes: 41 6e 6e c2 a0 4c 65 65"
       "PROBE contains U+00A0: true  contains ASCII space: false"
   - The guard exists at ws5_glide_persons_test.go:665-667, and nbspName is in the names
     list at :675.
   - The expected message is built from the name, so it holds the NBSP verbatim. Probe
     output: "41 6e 6e c2 a0 4c 65 65 20 6e 65 65 64 73 ...". Under M2a the log shows
     want "Ann Lee needs a birth month".
   - The case has teeth. N3 folds NBSP to a space in the handler's needs-a-birth-month
     message. It is KILLED by NamesXBirthMonths/Ann_Lee/empty#01.
   - N1 turns the NBSP into a space on the const line only. The guard fires:
     "ws5_glide_persons_test.go:666: nbspName must contain an actual NBSP".
   Missing:
   (a) No Go escape. A python byte count over the test file found 3 raw c2 a0 pairs and 0
       occurrences of ` `, ` `, `\xa0` or `\U000000a0`. The raw bytes are on:
         line 651: const nbspName = "Ann<NBSP>Lee"
         line 662: a comment
         line 665: strings.ContainsRune(nbspName, '<NBSP>'), where the guard's rune literal
                   is itself a raw NBSP
   (b) The guard is self-referential, so it survives the mutation it exists to catch.
       - N2 normalizes every NBSP in the test file to an ASCII space. That is the
         "editor / copy-paste" case the test's own comment names at :647-648 and :661-662.
         Result: exit=0, "ok budget2/internal/handlers/whatif", 0 failing lines. The guard
         is silent.
       - N2+N3: the normalized test file plus the NBSP-folding handler mutant. Run against
         the full packages (`-run .`): exit=0, "ok ... whatif 16.549s", "ok ... prepare".
       - So after one normalization pass the NBSP coverage is gone and nothing reports it.
   (c) The comment at :647 says "written with a \u escape so an editor or a copy-paste can
       never silently normalize it". That is false, and (b) shows the consequence.
   Needed: write the const as "Ann Lee" and the guard rune as ' ' (ASCII
   escapes). Then N2 has nothing to normalize, and a const-only edit trips the guard.

